  "item.animania.guide_book": "Animania Guide",
  "patchouli.animania.guide.landing": "Welcome to Animania! This guide covers the basics of raising and caring for the animals in this mod.",
  "patchouli.animania.category.getting_started.name": "Getting Started",
  "patchouli.animania.category.getting_started.description": "The basics: how animal care works in Animania.",
  "patchouli.animania.category.farm.name": "Farm Animals",
  "patchouli.animania.category.farm.description": "Chickens, cows, pigs, sheep, goats, horses, and everything that comes with them.",
  "patchouli.animania.category.extra.name": "Amphibians, Peafowl & Rodents",
  "patchouli.animania.category.extra.description": "Frogs, toads, peafowl, ferrets, hamsters, hedgehogs, and rabbits.",
  "patchouli.animania.category.catsdogs.name": "Cats & Dogs",
  "patchouli.animania.category.catsdogs.description": "Tameable companions with real breeds.",
  "patchouli.animania.entry.welcome.name": "Animal Care Basics",
  "patchouli.animania.entry.welcome.page1": "Most animals in Animania need three things to stay happy: food, water, and (for many species) sleep. You can tell an animal's status by watching how it behaves, or by looking at it with a compatible tooltip mod such as Jade, which shows Fed, Watered, and Sleeping status directly.$(br2)Feed an animal by right-clicking it with an item from its food list, or by filling a trough nearby - most animals will find and eat from a trough on their own.",
  "patchouli.animania.entry.welcome.page2": "Animals that can breed come in pairs: a male and a female. Feed both a food item while they're near each other and, if conditions are right, the female will become pregnant. After a gestation period she will give birth to a baby, which grows into an adult over time.$(br2)Some species (like peafowl and chickens) lay eggs into a nest instead of giving birth directly - the egg later hatches into a baby if a nest partner is nearby.",
  "patchouli.animania.entry.welcome.page3": "Many animals will sleep at night if they have a bed block (usually straw) nearby, and some can be put to sleep or woken by interacting with them. Sleeping animals are calmer and easier to work with, but won't respond to most other interactions until they wake up.$(br2)Tameable pets - ferrets, hamsters, dogs, and cats - are tamed by feeding them until they accept you as their owner. Once tamed, you can order them to sit by sneaking and right-clicking with an empty hand.",
  "patchouli.animania.entry.care_blocks.name": "Care Blocks",
  "patchouli.animania.entry.care_blocks.page1": "$(item)Straw$() is the simplest bed block - most animals will sleep on it at night if the game rule allows sleeping.$(br2)$(item)Trough$() The Trough holds both food and water. Fill it with a water bucket and drop in food items, and nearby hungry animals will help themselves automatically.",
  "patchouli.animania.entry.care_blocks.page2": "$(item)Nest$() is where egg-laying animals (chickens, peafowl) deposit their eggs. Leave an egg in a nest near a compatible male and it will eventually hatch.$(br2)$(item)Salt Lick$() keeps sheep and goats happy and healthy over time - place one where your flock can reach it.",
  "patchouli.animania.entry.farm_animals.name": "The Farmyard",
  "patchouli.animania.entry.farm_animals.page1": "Animania adds proper breeds for six classic farm animals: chickens, cows, pigs, sheep, goats, and horses. Each species has multiple real-world breeds with their own look and, in many cases, their own particular quirks - Rhode Island Red and Wyandotte hens lay brown eggs while other breeds lay white ones, for example.",
  "patchouli.animania.entry.farm_animals.page2": "Life stages matter: most species have a distinct male, female, and baby form, each a separate creature with its own model and behavior. Females of breeding age become pregnant and give birth to babies, which grow into adults over time. Shear sheep and Angora goats for wool, milk cows and goats by right-clicking with a bucket, and collect eggs from chicken and peafowl nests.",
  "patchouli.animania.entry.cheese.name": "Cheese Making",
  "patchouli.animania.entry.cheese.page1": "$(item)Cheese Mold$() turns milk into cheese over time. Fill it with milk from a cow, sheep, or goat (or with water, for a plain cheese), and it will slowly age.",
  "patchouli.animania.entry.cheese.page2": "Once aging finishes, break the mold's output to collect a wheel of cheese. Right-click the cheese block to eat a bite - each breed's milk produces a slightly different cheese with its own effect when eaten.",
  "patchouli.animania.entry.beekeeping.name": "Beekeeping",
  "patchouli.animania.entry.beekeeping.page1": "$(item)Hive$() Place a Hive to start collecting honey over time. Wild hives can also be found growing naturally near logs in forest, jungle, savanna, and badlands biomes - keep an eye out for them while exploring.",
  "patchouli.animania.entry.beekeeping.page2": "Right-click a hive with a glass bottle or bucket to collect honey once enough has accumulated. Shift-right-click to check how much honey is currently stored without taking any.",
  "patchouli.animania.entry.pullables.name": "Carts, Wagons & Tillers",
  "patchouli.animania.entry.pullables.page1": "$(item)Cart$() is a simple pullable storage vehicle. Attach a vanilla chest to an empty cart (shift-right-click with the chest in hand) to give it 36 slots of storage you can access any time by right-clicking.",
  "patchouli.animania.entry.pullables.page2": "The Wagon is a larger, permanent vehicle with 54 slots of storage, room for two passengers, and can even be slept in like a bed to skip the night. The Tiller is a third pullable implement for working the fields.",
  "patchouli.animania.entry.amphibians.name": "Frogs, Dart Frogs & Toads",
  "patchouli.animania.entry.amphibians.page1": "These small amphibians live near water and don't need feeding or breeding management like the larger animals - they're mostly decorative, adding life to ponds and wetlands. Dart frogs come in several bright warning colors.",
  "patchouli.animania.entry.peafowl.name": "Peafowl",
  "patchouli.animania.entry.peafowl.page1": "Peafowl come in seven colors: Blue, White, Taupe, Purple, Peach, Opal, and Charcoal. Like chickens, they have separate male (peacock), female (peahen), and chick forms, breed via nests, and can be fed and watered like any other farm animal.",
  "patchouli.animania.entry.rodents.name": "Small Pets",
  "patchouli.animania.entry.rodents.page1": "Ferrets (grey or white) and hedgehogs (normal or albino) are tameable pets that hunt pests like silverfish and will raid chicken nests for eggs when hungry. Hamsters come in nine colors and store food in their cheeks, visibly puffing out as they hoard more.",
  "patchouli.animania.entry.rodents.page2": "Rabbits are the one exception with a full breeding cycle like the farm animals - eight breeds, each with a buck, doe, and kit. Once a ferret or hamster is tamed, sneak and right-click it with an empty hand to tuck it into your pocket; sneak and right-click a block to set it back down.",
  "patchouli.animania.entry.dogs.name": "Dogs",
  "patchouli.animania.entry.dogs.page1": "Fifteen breeds are available, from tiny Chihuahuas to Great Danes, plus a Wolf-coated breed. Tame a dog by feeding it, then order it to sit by sneaking and right-clicking with an empty hand. Tamed dogs will defend their owner and follow them around.",
  "patchouli.animania.entry.dogs.page2": "German Shepherds have one more trick: nearby sheep and goats will follow wherever a tame, awake German Shepherd is currently headed, giving you a simple way to herd a flock from place to place.",
  "patchouli.animania.entry.cats.name": "Cats",
  "patchouli.animania.entry.cats.page1": "Eight breeds are available, from common Tabbies to fluffy Ragdolls. Cats are tamed the same way as dogs - feed them, then sneak-right-click with an empty hand to toggle sitting. Tamed cats will hunt silverfish that wander too close.",
  "jei.animania.cheese_mold.info": "Fill with milk (or water, for a plain cheese) using a bucket. The mold will slowly age its contents into a wheel of cheese over time - break it once aging finishes to collect the result.",
  "jei.animania.trough.info": "Fill with a water bucket and drop in food items. Hungry animals within range will eat and drink from the trough automatically.",
  "jei.animania.nest.info": "Egg-laying animals such as chickens and peafowl will deposit eggs here on their own. Left undisturbed near a compatible male, an egg will eventually hatch into a baby.",
  "jei.animania.hive.info": "Collects honey over time. Right-click with a glass bottle or bucket to harvest it once enough has accumulated, or shift-right-click to check the current amount without taking any.",
  "tooltip.animania.regeneration_ii_5_seconds": "Regeneration II (0:05)",
  "tooltip.animania.edible_anytime": "Edible anytime"
}
